## 🛠️ Setup

### 📦 Install dependencies and dev tools

This project uses [uv](https://github.com/astral-sh/uv) for dependency and virtual environment management.
Run the following command to install all project dependencies, including local development tools (ruff, mypy, pre-commit, alembic, etc.):

```bash
uv sync
```

{%- if add_pre_commit %}
### 🪝 Enable pre-commit hooks

```bash
uv run pre-commit install
```
{%- endif %}

### 🐍 Python Dependencies

Add a new package:

```bash
uv add <package_name>
# Examples: uv add pandas / uv add pytest --dev
```

Remove a package:

```bash
uv remove <package_name>
```

⚠️ Important: Do not use legacy commands like `uv pip install` or manually create environments with `uv venv`. The `uv add` and `uv remove` commands automatically keep `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`, and your virtual environment in sync.

## ▶️ Run the local stack (API + PostgreSQL)

Start the services using Docker Compose:

```bash
docker compose up
```

Once the API is running, access the FastAPI Swagger UI at:

- 📖 Docs: `http://localhost:8000/docs`

{%- if use_oidc and oidc_provider == 'Local Keycloak' %}
### 🔐 Local Keycloak login

If you selected Local Keycloak, you can log in to your frontend with these predefined accounts:

- `test_user` (password: `password`) - role `user`
- `test_admin` (password: `password`) - role `admin`

To administer Keycloak locally, open:

- `http://localhost:9080/admin`

Admin credentials:

- username: `admin`
- password: `admin`
{%- endif %}

## 🗄️ Database migrations workflow

You must use Alembic inside your running container using the provided Makefile commands.

Create a new revision from model changes:

```bash
make alembic-autogenerate m="your_migration_message"
```

Create a manual revision:

```bash
make alembic-revision m="your_manual_message"
```

Apply pending migrations:

```bash
make alembic-migrate
```

